WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
At the seaside.

00:12.000 --> 00:12.950
A cup of tea.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
Yes, dear.

00:18.000 --> 00:19.950
Here you are.

00:20.000 --> 00:20.950
Yes, dear.

00:21.000 --> 00:22.950
Here you are.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.000
Yes, dear.

00:31.000 --> 00:33.950
Would you like some jam, mother?

00:34.000 --> 00:35.950
I don't like ham, Nancy.

00:36.000 --> 00:37.950
You know I don't eat meat.

00:38.000 --> 00:39.950
You said jam, mother.

00:40.000 --> 00:40.950
Not ham.

00:41.000 --> 00:42.950
Would you like some jam, mother?

00:43.000 --> 00:44.950
Yes, please, Nancy.

00:45.000 --> 00:46.950
I hope it's strawberry jam.

00:47.000 --> 00:48.950
I like strawberry jam.

00:49.000 --> 00:50.950
I don't like raspberry jam.

00:51.000 --> 00:52.950
And I don't like plum jam.

00:53.000 --> 00:53.950
And I don't like...

00:54.000 --> 00:55.950
Yes, I know, mother.

00:56.000 --> 00:57.950
I only buy strawberry jam.

00:58.000 --> 01:01.950
Yes, strawberry jam for the last five years.

01:02.000 --> 01:02.950
Just for her.

01:03.000 --> 01:03.950
Not again.

01:04.000 --> 01:06.950
There are other people in this family, dear.

01:07.000 --> 01:08.950
I like raspberry jam.

01:09.000 --> 01:10.950
Well, you can do the shopping next week.

01:11.000 --> 01:12.950
And then you buy what you want.

01:13.000 --> 01:14.950
You know I have no time.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.950
No, dear.

01:17.000 --> 01:19.950
I don't like strawberry jam all the time.

01:20.000 --> 01:21.950
Not again.

01:22.000 --> 01:26.950
We're going on a nice family seaside holiday for a week.

01:27.000 --> 01:29.950
You can have raspberry jam for breakfast in the hotel.

01:30.000 --> 01:32.950
And mum can have strawberry jam, okay?

01:33.000 --> 01:33.950
Yes, dear.

01:34.000 --> 01:38.950
Oh, here you are, Boris.

01:39.000 --> 01:41.000
Have my jam sandwich.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.950
Don't give Boris your sandwich.

01:46.000 --> 01:47.950
You know what happens.

01:48.000 --> 01:49.950
He looks hungry.

01:50.000 --> 01:51.950
I don't think you give him enough food.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.950
It's not a horse, mum.

01:54.000 --> 01:55.950
It's not a real dog.

01:56.000 --> 01:58.950
A real dog is a golden retriever.

01:59.000 --> 02:01.950
I like golden retrievers.

02:02.000 --> 02:04.950
Boris is noisy and smelly.

02:05.000 --> 02:05.950
That reminds me.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.950
Why are we taking your mother on holiday?

02:09.000 --> 02:10.950
You know what happened last year?

02:11.000 --> 02:12.950
Not again, Pete.

02:13.000 --> 02:14.950
We can't leave her alone in the house.

02:15.000 --> 02:15.950
Why not?

02:16.000 --> 02:17.950
What's he saying about me?

02:18.000 --> 02:19.950
I know he's talking about me.

02:20.000 --> 02:21.950
I know he's talking about me.

02:22.000 --> 02:23.950
He doesn't like me.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.950
No, mother. It's okay.

02:26.000 --> 02:28.950
He's talking about the lovely holiday together.

02:29.000 --> 02:29.950
No, he's not.

02:30.000 --> 02:30.950
Yes, he is.

02:31.000 --> 02:31.950
No, I'm not.

02:32.000 --> 02:32.950
No, he's not.

02:33.000 --> 02:34.950
Yes, he is.

02:35.000 --> 02:36.950
I'll stop this, everyone.

02:37.000 --> 02:40.950
I want a nice, relaxing breakfast, please.

02:41.000 --> 02:42.950
We have a long journey today.

02:43.000 --> 02:47.000
Please try to be nice to each other for one minute.

02:48.000 --> 02:50.950
Not again. I can't believe it.

02:51.000 --> 02:52.950
Stop that, Josephine.

02:53.000 --> 02:54.950
It's not nice at the breakfast table.

02:55.000 --> 02:55.950
Why not?

02:56.000 --> 02:56.950
Because I say so.

02:57.000 --> 02:59.950
I tell you, every morning, not to do that.

03:00.000 --> 03:00.950
I want to.

03:01.000 --> 03:02.950
Robbie's hungry.

03:03.000 --> 03:05.950
You can feed it in your room in its cage.

03:06.000 --> 03:07.950
Please keep it in its cage.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.950
You get lonely.

03:10.000 --> 03:10.950
I don't know why.

03:11.000 --> 03:11.950
She has a pet rat.

03:12.000 --> 03:12.950
It's unhealthy.

03:13.000 --> 03:14.950
We said Josephine can have a pet.

03:15.000 --> 03:15.950
Don't you remember?

03:16.000 --> 03:17.950
Of course I remember.

03:18.000 --> 03:20.950
But a cat or a dog, not a parasite.

03:21.000 --> 03:22.950
I like Robbie.

03:23.000 --> 03:23.950
He's sweet.

03:24.000 --> 03:24.950
It smells.

03:25.000 --> 03:25.950
No, it doesn't.

03:26.000 --> 03:26.950
Yes, it does.

03:27.000 --> 03:28.950
I like Robbie.

03:29.000 --> 03:29.950
He's sweet.

03:30.000 --> 03:31.950
The rat is not coming on holiday.

03:32.000 --> 03:32.950
Why not?

03:33.000 --> 03:34.950
Because it's not.

03:35.000 --> 03:36.950
Nancy, speak to your daughter, please.

03:37.000 --> 03:38.950
Why is it always me?

03:39.000 --> 03:40.950
No, Josephine.

03:41.000 --> 03:41.950
It's not coming.

03:42.000 --> 03:43.950
It can't stay in the hotel.

03:44.000 --> 03:45.950
But I like Robbie.

03:46.000 --> 03:48.950
Be quiet, Mother.

03:49.000 --> 03:51.950
After breakfast, take it to your friend.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.950
She can look after it.

03:54.000 --> 03:55.950
But she's going out.

03:56.000 --> 03:57.950
Just do as I say, Josephine.

03:58.000 --> 03:59.950
Don't argue.

04:00.000 --> 04:00.950
I like him.

04:01.000 --> 04:02.950
He's sweet.

04:03.000 --> 04:03.950
Thank you, Grand.

04:04.000 --> 04:05.950
You see?

04:06.000 --> 04:06.950
Grandma.

04:07.000 --> 04:08.950
You see?

04:09.000 --> 04:10.950
Grand thinks Robbie is sweet.

04:11.000 --> 04:12.950
Maybe because it looks like her.

04:13.000 --> 04:14.950
He's talking about me again.

04:15.000 --> 04:16.950
What did he say, Nancy?

04:17.000 --> 04:18.950
It's not good for my heart.

04:19.000 --> 04:20.950
He knows I have high blood pressure.

04:21.000 --> 04:22.950
I said that it looks.

04:23.000 --> 04:23.950
Not again, Pete.

04:24.000 --> 04:27.950
The rat is not coming with us.

04:28.000 --> 04:30.950
You heard your mother, Josephine.

04:31.000 --> 04:31.950
I like him.

04:32.000 --> 04:32.950
It's sweet.

04:33.000 --> 04:35.950
I am getting very, very angry.

04:36.000 --> 04:38.950
You will find me in the garage cleaning the car.

04:39.000 --> 04:43.950
It is the only place in this house where I can find some peace and quiet.

04:44.000 --> 04:47.950
Why did you marry him, Nancy?

04:48.000 --> 04:50.950
Not again, Mum.

04:51.000 --> 04:52.950
I liked Jonathan.

04:53.000 --> 04:55.950
You know he lived next door.

04:56.000 --> 04:57.950
He liked you, too.

04:58.000 --> 04:59.950
He had very nice tea.

05:00.000 --> 05:02.950
He went to university.

05:03.000 --> 05:04.950
He's a doctor.

05:05.000 --> 05:06.950
Lovely house.

05:07.000 --> 05:08.950
I met his mother last week.

05:09.000 --> 05:10.950
He's...

05:11.000 --> 05:13.000
Not again, Mum.

05:21.000 --> 05:22.950
Go in your own room, Josephine.

05:23.000 --> 05:24.950
Pack your suitcase.

05:25.000 --> 05:26.950
I want to pack my bag now.

05:27.000 --> 05:28.950
I don't want to go on holiday.

05:29.000 --> 05:30.950
It's math.

05:31.000 --> 05:33.950
The same totally naff town.

05:34.000 --> 05:35.950
The same naff hotel.

05:36.000 --> 05:36.950
The same naff food.

05:37.000 --> 05:38.950
That's enough, Josephine.

05:39.000 --> 05:39.950
You are coming with the family.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.950
You're too young to stay at home alone.

05:43.000 --> 05:45.950
Why don't we go to Spain on Mallorca?

05:46.000 --> 05:48.950
All my friends go abroad.

05:49.000 --> 05:52.950
Why do we always go to bloody, stupid Blackpool?

05:53.000 --> 05:53.950
I hate it.

05:54.000 --> 05:58.950
I want to go to somewhere where I can chill out and meet some fit guys.

05:59.000 --> 06:00.950
Blackpool is nice.

06:01.000 --> 06:02.950
We can sit on the beach.

06:03.000 --> 06:04.950
We can go to the fair.

06:05.000 --> 06:06.950
We can ride on a donkey.

06:07.000 --> 06:07.950
We can have fun.

06:08.000 --> 06:09.950
I don't want to sodding donkey.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.950
Mum, I am 15 years old.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.950
I don't want to ride on a naffing donkey.

06:16.000 --> 06:18.950
I want to go to discos.

06:19.000 --> 06:19.950
Meet people.

06:20.000 --> 06:21.950
Have fun.

06:22.000 --> 06:23.950
No, this year it is Blackpool.

06:24.000 --> 06:24.950
That is final.

06:25.000 --> 06:27.950
No more arguments and stop using those terrible words.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.950
I say what I want.

06:30.000 --> 06:31.950
But why do we always go to Blackpool?

06:32.000 --> 06:33.950
Because...

06:34.000 --> 06:35.950
Because...

06:36.000 --> 06:38.950
Because we do.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.950
Don't take that dress, Mum. It's too short.

06:42.000 --> 06:43.950
I don't think it is.

06:44.000 --> 06:44.950
Yes, it is.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.950
Everyone can see your fat legs.

06:48.000 --> 06:49.950
I'm taking it.

06:50.000 --> 06:51.950
What's this?

06:52.000 --> 06:53.950
Why are you taking this?

06:54.000 --> 06:55.950
You never wear this for Dad.

06:56.000 --> 06:56.950
Is it new?

06:57.000 --> 06:57.950
Give it to me, Josephine.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.950
I bought it for the holiday.

07:00.000 --> 07:01.950
Does Dad know you bought it?

07:02.000 --> 07:03.950
Dad, Dad, come here.

07:04.000 --> 07:04.950
Stop it, Josephine.

07:05.000 --> 07:06.950
No, I didn't tell your father.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.950
It's a surprise.

07:10.000 --> 07:11.950
Why did you buy it?

07:12.000 --> 07:13.950
It looks very expensive.

07:14.000 --> 07:17.950
You are much too old to wear it.

07:18.000 --> 07:19.950
I know.

07:20.000 --> 07:22.950
It's that slimy Italian manager at the hotel.

07:23.000 --> 07:24.950
What's his name?

07:25.000 --> 07:26.950
I know.

07:27.000 --> 07:28.950
squeegee or something.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.950
I don't know what you're talking about, Josephine.

07:31.000 --> 07:32.950
Yes, you do.

07:33.000 --> 07:34.950
Italian manager, we meet every year.

07:35.000 --> 07:37.950
Oh, yes.

07:38.000 --> 07:40.950
His name is not squeegee.

07:41.000 --> 07:42.950
It's Luigi.

07:43.000 --> 07:45.950
Luigi Bertolini.

07:46.000 --> 07:47.950
And he's not slimy.

07:48.000 --> 07:49.950
He has charming and kind.

07:50.000 --> 07:51.950
I don't like him.

07:52.000 --> 07:53.950
He's got spots and he smells like a perfume factory.

07:54.000 --> 07:56.950
They're fickle, it's not spots.

07:57.000 --> 07:59.950
Did you do it with him last year, Mum?

08:00.000 --> 08:01.950
No, I didn't.

08:02.000 --> 08:04.950
What a thing to say.

08:05.000 --> 08:06.950
You know how much I love your father.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.950
Why do you say that, Josephine?

08:09.000 --> 08:10.950
No reason, Mum.

08:11.000 --> 08:12.950
No reason.

08:13.000 --> 08:15.950
It's just that I bought a new bikini for the holiday.

08:16.000 --> 08:17.950
What do you think?

08:18.000 --> 08:18.950
Oh!

08:19.000 --> 08:21.950
Oh, no, Mother.

08:22.000 --> 08:23.950
What's the matter?

08:24.000 --> 08:24.950
I like it.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.950
Red is a nice colour.

08:27.000 --> 08:30.950
The woman in the shop said that red is the colour for this year.

08:31.000 --> 08:33.950
It's not the colour that's the problem.

08:34.000 --> 08:35.950
So what's the matter then?

08:36.000 --> 08:38.950
The problem is the bikini, Mother.

08:39.000 --> 08:41.950
It's, um, very small.

08:42.000 --> 08:44.950
Yes, I want to get a suntan this year.

08:45.000 --> 08:47.950
It's Blackpool, Mother, not the Caribbean.

08:48.000 --> 08:50.950
It rained last year and the year before.

08:51.000 --> 08:54.950
But don't you think you're a bit old for that bikini?

08:55.000 --> 08:58.950
John at the Bingo Club said I have a good body.

08:59.000 --> 09:01.950
John? From across the road?

09:02.000 --> 09:04.950
He's totally blind. He has a white stick.

09:05.000 --> 09:05.950
Yes, I know.

09:06.000 --> 09:09.000
But he feels I have a great body.

09:12.000 --> 09:16.950
But a cloudier shiffer has a red bikini just like this one.

09:17.000 --> 09:18.950
I saw it on television.

09:19.000 --> 09:21.950
Mother, you cannot wear that.

09:22.000 --> 09:24.950
It's super grand.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.950
Don't listen to Nancy.

09:28.000 --> 09:31.950
Oh, please, wear it on the beach and tell me what happens.

09:32.000 --> 09:33.950
Don't say that, Josephine.

09:34.000 --> 09:35.950
She's too old to wear that.

09:36.000 --> 09:37.950
I like it.

09:38.000 --> 09:40.950
I hope the young men on the beach like it too.

09:41.000 --> 09:44.950
Oh, dear Mother, you get worse as you get older.

09:45.000 --> 09:46.950
Please go and finish your packing.

09:47.000 --> 09:48.950
We're all ready late.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.950
Pete gets angry if we're late.

09:51.000 --> 09:52.950
Yes, dear, yes, dear.

09:53.000 --> 09:55.950
Just a few more things to pack.

09:56.000 --> 09:59.950
Oh, this tender thing is a bit uncomfortable.

10:00.000 --> 10:02.950
Does it look all right from behind?

10:03.000 --> 10:03.950
No, it doesn't.

10:04.000 --> 10:04.950
Oh, it looks fun.

10:05.000 --> 10:07.950
Fantastic, grand.

10:08.000 --> 10:10.950
Go and ask Dad what he thinks.

10:11.000 --> 10:13.950
That's a good idea.

10:14.000 --> 10:14.950
He's a man.

10:15.000 --> 10:16.950
No, it's not a good idea, Mum.

10:17.000 --> 10:19.000
Josephine is joking.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.950
Pete, come into the house, please.

10:32.000 --> 10:33.950
Our suitcases are ready.

10:34.000 --> 10:36.950
I think my mother is ready too.

10:37.000 --> 10:38.950
Okay, the car's ready.

10:39.000 --> 10:41.950
The engine sounds fantastic.

10:42.000 --> 10:44.000
No problems.

10:46.000 --> 10:47.950
I'm not so sure.

10:48.000 --> 10:50.950
It's my mother, Rick, with her bag.

10:51.000 --> 10:51.950
Yes?

10:52.000 --> 10:53.950
So she is coming with us.

10:54.000 --> 10:55.950
Of course she is.

10:56.000 --> 10:58.950
Super terrific, fantastic.

10:59.000 --> 11:02.000
I am so happy.

11:16.000 --> 11:23.950
Can I come in?

11:24.000 --> 11:24.950
Are you ready?

11:25.000 --> 11:26.950
I want to take your bag.

11:27.000 --> 11:28.950
You want to take me back?

11:29.000 --> 11:30.950
No, don't.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.950
I don't want to go back there.

11:33.000 --> 11:33.950
Not there.

11:34.000 --> 11:35.950
Nancy said I can stay here.

11:36.000 --> 11:36.950
What?

11:37.000 --> 11:37.950
What are you talking about?

11:38.000 --> 11:38.950
Nancy, stop him.

11:39.000 --> 11:40.950
He wants to take me back.

11:41.000 --> 11:42.950
I don't know what you're talking about.

11:43.000 --> 11:44.950
Please stay, don't send me back.

11:45.000 --> 11:45.950
Shut up, please.

11:46.000 --> 11:50.950
All I said was that I want to take your B-A-G bag.

11:51.000 --> 11:51.950
Bag!

11:52.000 --> 11:53.950
What's the problem now?

11:54.000 --> 11:55.950
He wants to take me back.

11:56.000 --> 11:56.950
He doesn't like me.

11:57.000 --> 11:58.950
Why did you say that, Pete?

11:59.000 --> 12:01.950
Why did you always upset my mother?

12:02.000 --> 12:05.950
All I said to the old fossil was that I want to take her bag.

12:06.000 --> 12:06.950
Bag!

12:07.000 --> 12:09.950
I am not an old fossil.

12:10.000 --> 12:14.950
Robert, a friend at the Bingo Club said I look like Marilyn Monroe.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.950
Robert thinks everyone looks like her.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.950
Last week he called me, Marilyn.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.950
Stop it, both of you.

12:21.000 --> 12:24.950
Take her suitcase, Pete, and then collect Joses.

12:25.000 --> 12:26.950
What is in this suitcase?

12:27.000 --> 12:28.950
It's so heavy.

12:29.000 --> 12:30.950
Are you stealing our silver?

12:31.000 --> 12:32.950
Don't start again, Pete.

12:33.000 --> 12:33.950
I'm going.

12:34.000 --> 12:36.000
I'm going.

12:40.000 --> 12:41.950
It's too loud.

12:42.000 --> 12:43.950
Stop playing now, Josephine.

12:44.000 --> 12:45.950
Turn it down.

12:46.000 --> 12:47.950
What a noise.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.950
Stop playing.

12:50.000 --> 12:51.950
What do you say, Dad?

12:52.000 --> 12:53.950
I said, turn it down.

12:54.000 --> 12:55.950
Oh.

12:56.000 --> 12:56.950
You have.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.950
Why do you play that terrible music, Josephine?

13:00.000 --> 13:01.950
I think it's great.

13:02.000 --> 13:04.950
It's what I want to do to write music.

13:05.000 --> 13:07.950
You think you can make a living with that kind of music?

13:08.000 --> 13:09.950
Well, I was young.

13:10.000 --> 13:11.950
They knew how to write music.

13:12.000 --> 13:13.950
And the words were important.

13:14.000 --> 13:14.950
And now...

13:15.000 --> 13:15.950
Yes, Dad.

13:16.000 --> 13:16.950
I know.

13:17.000 --> 13:17.950
You tell me every day.

13:18.000 --> 13:18.950
When you get older.

13:19.000 --> 13:19.950
Oh, yes.

13:20.000 --> 13:20.950
Same old story.

13:21.000 --> 13:21.950
Shut up.

13:22.000 --> 13:23.950
I'm not interested.

13:24.000 --> 13:26.950
I don't want any arguments on holiday.

13:27.000 --> 13:29.950
This is the only time your mother and I can relax.

13:30.000 --> 13:32.950
I don't want any problems, Josephine.

13:33.000 --> 13:35.950
Come with me and bring your suitcase to the car now.

13:36.000 --> 13:36.950
Now.

13:37.000 --> 13:38.950
Naff, Blackpool.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.950
Boring family.

13:41.000 --> 13:41.950
Boring life.

13:42.000 --> 13:43.000
I hate it.

13:49.000 --> 13:49.950
Hurry up, Nancy.

13:50.000 --> 13:50.950
Get in the car.

13:51.000 --> 13:51.950
We're waiting.

13:52.000 --> 13:52.950
Just wait a minute, dear.

13:53.000 --> 13:54.950
Graham isn't here.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.950
You don't want to go without her, do you?

13:58.000 --> 13:59.950
I said you don't want to go without her.

14:00.000 --> 14:00.950
I heard you.

14:01.000 --> 14:01.950
No.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.950
I don't want to go without her.

14:04.000 --> 14:05.950
But perhaps we could try it.

14:06.000 --> 14:08.950
Be honest to a dear for once in your life.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.950
We're all the family she has now.

14:12.000 --> 14:12.950
Yes, dear.

14:13.000 --> 14:14.950
But where is she?

14:15.000 --> 14:16.950
Get off, Boris.

14:17.000 --> 14:17.950
Stop it.

14:18.000 --> 14:19.950
Don't get Morris excited.

14:20.000 --> 14:22.950
You know what happens if he gets too excited.

14:23.000 --> 14:23.950
Stop it, Morris.

14:24.000 --> 14:25.950
Don't do that.

14:26.000 --> 14:26.950
Oh.

14:27.000 --> 14:27.950
No.

14:28.000 --> 14:29.950
What's wrong, Pete?

14:30.000 --> 14:32.950
What's that smell?

14:33.000 --> 14:34.950
Why do we keep this dog?

14:35.000 --> 14:35.950
Get off me.

14:36.000 --> 14:37.950
Look what he's done.

14:38.000 --> 14:38.950
Oh.

14:39.000 --> 14:41.950
Now I have to change my shirt.

14:42.000 --> 14:43.950
What a family.

14:44.000 --> 14:46.950
Wonderful start to the holiday.

14:47.000 --> 14:47.950
Why?

14:48.000 --> 14:48.950
Oh, what?

14:49.000 --> 14:51.950
Boris was sick on Dad's shirt.

14:52.000 --> 14:54.000
It's not funny, Jessica.

14:56.000 --> 14:57.950
Boris, come here. Sit quietly.

14:58.000 --> 14:59.950
You're a bad dog.

15:00.000 --> 15:01.000
Here I am.

15:04.000 --> 15:05.950
Oh.

15:06.000 --> 15:07.950
Where's your husband Nancy?

15:08.000 --> 15:09.950
He's always late.

15:10.000 --> 15:10.950
Oh.

15:11.000 --> 15:12.950
What's that smell?

15:13.000 --> 15:13.950
Is it Pete?

15:14.000 --> 15:14.950
It smells.

15:15.000 --> 15:15.950
Yes, Mother.

15:16.000 --> 15:16.950
Thank you.

15:17.000 --> 15:18.950
Boris was sick on Pete.

15:19.000 --> 15:20.950
He's changing his shirt.

15:21.000 --> 15:22.950
I don't know why you married him, Nancy.

15:23.000 --> 15:25.950
What's that noise?

15:26.000 --> 15:30.000
Have you got that rat with you, Josephine?

15:31.000 --> 15:31.950
Oh, no.

15:32.000 --> 15:33.950
Your father told you not to bring it.

15:34.000 --> 15:35.950
I know, Mum.

15:36.000 --> 15:38.950
But I want Robbie to come on a holiday.

15:39.000 --> 15:40.950
He's very quiet.

15:41.000 --> 15:42.950
Please don't tell Dad.

15:43.000 --> 15:43.950
Please.

15:44.000 --> 15:44.950
I like him.

15:45.000 --> 15:45.950
He's sweet.

15:46.000 --> 15:46.950
Please, Mum.

15:47.000 --> 15:48.950
Promise not to say anything.

15:49.000 --> 15:49.950
Please.

15:50.000 --> 15:51.950
I'm not happy, Josephine.

15:52.000 --> 15:53.950
Your father said no.

15:54.000 --> 15:56.950
When he finds out that you have that rat with you.

15:57.000 --> 15:58.950
I hate pets.

15:59.000 --> 16:00.950
Why do we keep it?

16:01.000 --> 16:01.950
I like him.

16:02.000 --> 16:02.950
He's sweet.

16:03.000 --> 16:05.950
It's loud and too expensive.

16:06.000 --> 16:08.950
I don't know what you mean.

16:09.000 --> 16:12.950
He's always very quiet and he costs nothing to feed.

16:13.000 --> 16:17.950
Josephine, show him what are you talking about, Gran.

16:18.000 --> 16:19.950
You gave it a jam sandwich at the breakfast table.

16:20.000 --> 16:22.950
I didn't feed him at the breakfast table.

16:23.000 --> 16:23.950
Yes, you did.

16:24.000 --> 16:24.950
I saw you.

16:25.000 --> 16:26.950
You fed it a strawberry sandwich.

16:27.000 --> 16:28.950
No, I didn't.

16:29.000 --> 16:30.950
Please tell him Nancy.

16:31.000 --> 16:32.950
Don't ask Nancy.

16:33.000 --> 16:34.950
I think your mother is losing her memory.

16:35.000 --> 16:37.950
Perhaps an old people's home is the place for her now.

16:38.000 --> 16:39.950
He doesn't like me, Nancy.

16:40.000 --> 16:42.950
He wants to put me into a home.

16:43.000 --> 16:44.950
I always knew he didn't like me.

16:45.000 --> 16:46.950
Both of you be quiet.

16:47.000 --> 16:49.950
I'm getting one of my headaches.

16:50.000 --> 16:53.950
I just want a few days of relaxation.

16:54.000 --> 16:55.950
Everyone be quiet.

16:56.000 --> 16:58.950
It wasn't my fault, wasn't it?

16:59.000 --> 17:01.950
You can't wear that t-shirt, dear.

17:02.000 --> 17:05.950
It's too small and I can see your stomach.

17:06.000 --> 17:07.950
It looks good.

17:08.000 --> 17:09.950
I always wear it on holiday.

17:10.000 --> 17:12.950
I know, dear, but it's very old.

17:13.000 --> 17:14.950
You have other new t-shirts.

17:15.000 --> 17:17.950
I know, but this is my favourite.

17:18.000 --> 17:22.950
Do you think a t-shirt with a picture of Cliff Richard on it is alright?

17:23.000 --> 17:26.950
We are staying at the Grand Park Hotel.

17:27.000 --> 17:29.950
I don't think it's a good idea.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.950
It's my holiday as well.

17:32.000 --> 17:33.950
I think it's great.

17:34.000 --> 17:35.950
I like Cliff Richard.

17:36.000 --> 17:37.950
He's a nice man.

17:38.000 --> 17:41.950
Why didn't you marry someone like Cliff Richard, Nancy?

17:42.000 --> 17:45.950
He's got a lovely smile and lovely teeth.

17:46.000 --> 17:49.950
Oh, a summer holiday, summer holiday.

17:50.000 --> 17:54.000
One day some, one day some, one day.

18:00.000 --> 18:02.950
Is this car okay?

18:03.000 --> 18:05.000
Of course, no problems.

18:07.000 --> 18:08.950
Are we ready now? Can we go?

18:09.000 --> 18:11.950
Wait a minute, I must go to the toilet again.

18:12.000 --> 18:14.000
Just wait a minute please.

18:16.000 --> 18:17.000
Oh no.

18:18.000 --> 18:20.950
I don't want to stop every ten minutes for your mother.

18:21.000 --> 18:24.950
Nancy, we have 250 miles to drive today.

18:25.000 --> 18:27.950
I hope this piece of junk can go 250 miles.

18:28.000 --> 18:30.950
No problem, trust me.

18:31.000 --> 18:33.950
Sometimes I think you don't trust me dear.

18:34.000 --> 18:39.000
No, you're right. I don't trust you.

18:43.000 --> 18:46.000
I'm okay. We can go.

18:47.000 --> 18:48.950
Last, last, last, last.

18:49.000 --> 18:51.000
APPLAUSE

19:12.000 --> 19:16.950
12 hours to drive 250 miles.

19:17.000 --> 19:19.950
It's now nearly midnight.

19:20.000 --> 19:22.950
I'm hungry. I want a burger.

19:23.000 --> 19:25.950
Oh, that's a good idea, Josie.

19:26.000 --> 19:27.950
I want one too.

19:28.000 --> 19:31.950
What a terrible journey. It was worse than last year.

19:32.000 --> 19:32.950
Yes, but...

19:33.000 --> 19:35.950
This is the last holiday we come in that car.

19:36.000 --> 19:36.950
Yes.

19:37.000 --> 19:41.950
I am not coming to Blackpool again in a car that breaks down every 20 miles.

19:42.000 --> 19:42.950
Yes.

19:43.000 --> 19:44.950
I'm hungry. I want a burger.

19:45.000 --> 19:47.950
With chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

19:48.000 --> 19:49.950
How are you trying to say, Pete?

19:50.000 --> 19:52.950
Yes, but nothing, dear.

19:53.000 --> 19:54.950
I want a new car.

19:55.000 --> 19:55.950
Yes.

19:56.000 --> 19:57.950
All my friends laugh when they see us in that car.

19:58.000 --> 19:59.950
It's quicker by bike.

20:00.000 --> 20:01.950
And a medium collar.

20:02.000 --> 20:04.950
No, a large one. I am on holiday.

20:05.000 --> 20:07.950
Yes, but it is a classic car.

20:08.000 --> 20:09.950
What's wrong with it?

20:10.000 --> 20:16.950
It is old, unreliable, uncomfortable, noisy, smelly, expensive.

20:17.000 --> 20:19.950
I hate the color. I hate it.

20:20.000 --> 20:21.950
Do you understand?

20:22.000 --> 20:23.950
So, you don't like it, dear?

20:24.000 --> 20:26.950
No. I don't like it.

20:27.000 --> 20:28.950
Do you ever listen to me?

20:29.000 --> 20:29.950
Sorry?

20:30.000 --> 20:30.950
I don't.

20:31.000 --> 20:32.950
I'm hungry. I want a burger.

20:33.000 --> 20:34.950
You're quiet, Josie. Not now.

20:35.000 --> 20:37.950
We can buy you a burger as well, Nancy.

20:38.000 --> 20:39.950
Thank you, Mum.

20:40.000 --> 20:42.950
Burgers are not healthy. I'm on a diet.

20:43.000 --> 20:47.950
You're always on a diet. You still look fat.

20:48.000 --> 20:50.950
Come here, Boris. Come here. Don't do that.

20:51.000 --> 20:52.950
No. Catch him.

20:53.000 --> 20:54.950
Why did you let him go?

20:55.000 --> 20:58.950
I didn't let him go. He escaped through the car window.

20:59.000 --> 21:02.950
He's run onto the beach. I can hear him jumping in the waves.

21:03.000 --> 21:04.950
You can go and get him, Pete.

21:05.000 --> 21:06.950
Yes, dear. But why me?

21:07.000 --> 21:09.950
You are the man of the family, aren't you?

21:10.000 --> 21:11.950
Sometimes I'm not so sure.

21:12.000 --> 21:13.950
What do you mean, Nancy?

21:14.000 --> 21:17.950
Nothing, dear. I suppose it happens when you get older.

21:18.000 --> 21:18.950
What happened?

21:19.000 --> 21:22.950
Nothing. Anyway, what about Boris?

21:23.000 --> 21:25.950
We can talk later.

21:26.000 --> 21:29.950
Josephine? Nancy? Gran? Can you come and help me?

21:30.000 --> 21:32.950
Thank you, everyone.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.950
Wonderful, all family.

21:36.000 --> 21:38.950
I'm hungry. I want a burger.

21:39.000 --> 21:41.950
With chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

21:42.000 --> 21:46.950
It's nearly midnight, and all you two can think about is a burger.

21:47.000 --> 21:50.950
The burger shop is over there. I can see it. Five minutes and we're back.

21:51.000 --> 21:53.950
Come on, Gran. We're going.

21:54.000 --> 21:55.950
Have you got some money, Gran?

21:56.000 --> 22:00.950
Yes, but I want a double portion of chips and lots of tomato ketchup.

22:01.000 --> 22:04.950
No problem, Gran. If you're paying.

22:05.000 --> 22:06.950
You can have what you want.

22:07.000 --> 22:08.950
Josephine?

22:09.000 --> 22:12.950
I want two burgers. I'm so hungry. I could eat Boris.

22:13.000 --> 22:13.950
One.

22:14.000 --> 22:17.950
Perhaps I can have a small burger as well.

22:18.000 --> 22:19.950
It is my holiday.

22:20.000 --> 22:21.950
One burger won't hurt my diet.

22:22.000 --> 22:23.950
But I don't want any chips and ketchup.

22:24.000 --> 22:26.950
Well done, Nancy. You only live once.

22:27.000 --> 22:28.950
It's about five minutes, Mum.

22:29.000 --> 22:31.950
Come on, Gran. Ooh, not so fast.

22:32.000 --> 22:34.950
You know I have a bad leg.

22:35.000 --> 22:37.950
It's Dad's birthday on Wednesday.

22:38.000 --> 22:39.950
Do you have a present for him?

22:40.000 --> 22:40.950
No.

22:41.000 --> 22:41.950
Do you?

22:42.000 --> 22:42.950
No.

22:43.000 --> 22:45.950
I never know what to buy him.

22:46.000 --> 22:47.950
I can't be bothered.

22:48.000 --> 22:51.950
Mum always buys something for me to give him. It's easier.

22:52.000 --> 22:53.950
Dad doesn't know.

22:54.000 --> 22:55.950
Nancy does the same for me.

22:56.000 --> 22:59.000
I never know what to get your father either.

23:00.000 --> 23:02.950
Oh, but what can we do for him this year?

23:03.000 --> 23:04.950
Something a bit different.

23:05.000 --> 23:06.950
And a bit shocking.

23:07.000 --> 23:09.950
What about a new Cliff Richard T-shirt?

23:10.000 --> 23:10.950
Oh.

23:11.000 --> 23:11.950
It's Naph.

23:12.000 --> 23:14.950
What about a stripper?

23:15.000 --> 23:17.950
Cool idea.

23:18.000 --> 23:20.950
But aren't they expensive?

23:21.000 --> 23:22.950
I wonder what Mum thinks.

23:23.000 --> 23:24.950
Don't tell your Mum.

23:25.000 --> 23:27.950
It's a surprise for both of them.

23:28.000 --> 23:30.950
Don't worry about the money I have enough with me.

23:31.000 --> 23:33.950
That's cool.

23:34.000 --> 23:34.950
What type of stripper?

23:35.000 --> 23:36.950
Leave it to me, Josie.

23:37.000 --> 23:37.950
Leave it to me.

23:38.000 --> 23:39.950
Oh, great. Well done, Gran.

23:40.000 --> 23:41.950
Oh, here we are.

23:42.000 --> 23:44.950
Now, don't forget, I want a double burger.

23:45.000 --> 23:48.950
No, a double cheese burger with extra chips.

23:49.000 --> 23:52.950
Oh, and do you think your Dad wants a burger as well?

23:53.000 --> 23:54.950
Don't waste your money.

23:55.000 --> 23:58.000
Save it to the stripper.

24:00.000 --> 24:06.000
Anyway, I think he's too busy at the moment, chasing Boris through the waves.

24:13.000 --> 24:15.950
Where is that, Doc? I can't find him.

24:16.000 --> 24:18.950
We're not waiting in this car any longer, Pete.

24:19.000 --> 24:22.000
It's getting cold and I want my bed.

24:23.000 --> 24:25.950
So come on, get the luggage and we can check in.

24:26.000 --> 24:29.950
Okay. Okay, I can look for him later, I suppose.

24:30.000 --> 24:31.950
What a day.

24:32.000 --> 24:35.950
You can look for him if you want. I'm tired.

24:36.000 --> 24:37.950
What's that smell?

24:38.000 --> 24:39.950
What are you eating, Josie?

24:40.000 --> 24:41.950
A burger.

24:42.000 --> 24:45.950
You too, Gran, and Nancy, you are all eating.

24:46.000 --> 24:48.950
Where is my burger? I'm so hungry.

24:49.000 --> 24:51.950
Sorry, we forgot to get you one.

24:52.000 --> 24:53.950
You didn't say you wanted a burger.

24:54.000 --> 24:56.950
That's because I wasn't here.

24:57.000 --> 25:01.950
I was running up and down the beach in the dark, looking for that stupid dog.

25:02.000 --> 25:03.950
I fell over twice.

25:04.000 --> 25:05.950
The couples were very angry.

25:06.000 --> 25:07.950
It was embarrassing.

25:08.000 --> 25:11.000
They were, um, busy.

25:14.000 --> 25:15.950
Oh, wait a minute.

25:16.000 --> 25:18.950
A biscuit at the bottom of my handbag.

25:19.000 --> 25:20.950
Um, oh, yes, here it is.

25:21.000 --> 25:23.950
Oh, thank you very much.

25:24.000 --> 25:25.950
Nice of you to think of me.

25:26.000 --> 25:27.950
Oh, how wonderful.

25:28.000 --> 25:28.950
One biscuit.

25:29.000 --> 25:30.950
Not even a chocolate biscuit.

25:31.000 --> 25:33.950
Just a plain, boring, tasteless biscuit.

25:34.000 --> 25:36.950
I hope I can sleep tonight on such a full stomach.

25:37.000 --> 25:39.950
There's no need to be so sarcastic.

25:40.000 --> 25:42.950
Oh, it tastes terrible.

25:43.000 --> 25:43.950
What is it?

25:44.000 --> 25:45.950
Maybe to me, Pete.

25:46.000 --> 25:47.950
Now, where are my glasses?

25:48.000 --> 25:49.950
Oh, I can't find them.

25:50.000 --> 25:52.950
What does it say on the packet, Nancy?

25:53.000 --> 25:55.950
Wonderful, woofy biscuits.

25:56.000 --> 25:57.950
It's a dog biscuit.

25:58.000 --> 25:59.950
A dog biscuit?

26:00.000 --> 26:01.950
I ate a dog biscuit.

26:02.000 --> 26:04.950
I think I need a doctor.

26:05.000 --> 26:05.950
I suddenly feel real.

26:06.000 --> 26:06.950
Oh, don't worry.

26:07.000 --> 26:07.950
It's OK.

26:08.000 --> 26:11.000
When you start barking, I can ask for a doctor.

26:12.000 --> 26:12.950
Come on.

26:13.000 --> 26:15.000
Let's go into the hotel.

26:23.000 --> 26:26.950
Oh, good evening, Mr. and Mrs. Britain and family.

26:27.000 --> 26:29.950
Oh, hello, Mr. Bertolini.

26:30.000 --> 26:31.950
Luigi.

26:32.000 --> 26:33.950
Lovely to see you again.

26:34.000 --> 26:34.950
How are you?

26:35.000 --> 26:36.950
I'm fine.

26:37.000 --> 26:37.950
And you?

26:38.000 --> 26:39.950
Oh, we're all fine.

26:40.000 --> 26:40.950
Thank you.

26:41.000 --> 26:44.950
It's so nice to be here in your lovely hotel.

26:45.000 --> 26:48.950
You are looking younger than last year, Nancy.

26:49.000 --> 26:50.950
Do you think so?

26:51.000 --> 26:53.950
Oh, thank you so much.

26:54.000 --> 26:58.950
I made a reservation for two double rooms with a bathroom for one week.

26:59.000 --> 27:01.950
Eh, but I don't understand.

27:02.000 --> 27:03.950
You are one week early?

27:04.000 --> 27:06.950
You have a booking from next Saturday, not today.

27:07.000 --> 27:08.950
No, that is wrong.

27:09.000 --> 27:12.950
I phoned two months ago and booked seven nights for this week.

27:13.000 --> 27:14.950
No, I'm sorry, Mr. Britain.

27:15.000 --> 27:19.950
I answered the phone myself and I put it into the computer system immediately.

27:20.000 --> 27:20.950
Oh, no.

27:21.000 --> 27:22.950
I can't believe it.

27:23.000 --> 27:23.950
There must be some escape.

27:24.000 --> 27:25.950
I hope so.

27:26.000 --> 27:28.950
I am not going home at this time.

27:29.000 --> 27:31.950
I'm sure it isn't a problem, is it?

27:32.000 --> 27:33.950
Eh, let me see.

27:34.000 --> 27:37.950
I am sorry, but we only have one spare room at the moment.

27:38.000 --> 27:39.950
We are almost fully booked tonight.

27:40.000 --> 27:41.950
We have a wedding party.

27:42.000 --> 27:42.950
That's okay.

27:43.000 --> 27:45.950
My wife and daughter and I can have the one room.

27:46.000 --> 27:49.950
My wife's mother can sleep on some chairs in the hotel bar.

27:50.000 --> 27:53.950
Look, if she gets thirsty in the night, she can have a drink or two.

27:54.000 --> 27:54.950
My side?

27:55.000 --> 27:56.950
Don't you think, Graham?

27:57.000 --> 27:57.950
Makes you happy?

27:58.000 --> 27:58.950
Stop it, Peter.

27:59.000 --> 28:00.950
Mum is not sleeping in the bar.

28:01.000 --> 28:02.950
I am not sleeping in the bar.

28:03.000 --> 28:06.950
I have a bad back, and my plumbing is not so good.

28:07.000 --> 28:08.950
Mum is only joking.

28:09.000 --> 28:10.950
There is a bed for you.

28:11.000 --> 28:12.950
Of course I was only joking.

28:13.000 --> 28:15.950
Maybe you have a cupboard somewhere in the cellar?

28:16.000 --> 28:16.950
No.

28:17.000 --> 28:18.950
Mum is in the room with Josie and myself.

28:19.000 --> 28:21.950
You, Pete, can find somewhere else to sleep.

28:22.000 --> 28:22.950
What?

28:23.000 --> 28:23.950
No!

28:24.000 --> 28:26.950
It was your job to book the hotel.

28:27.000 --> 28:29.950
I can't get you to do a simple job like that.

28:30.000 --> 28:32.950
You made the mistake, so it's your problem.

28:33.000 --> 28:34.950
Where do I go?

28:35.000 --> 28:36.950
You can find another hotel.

28:37.000 --> 28:37.950
You can sleep on the beach.

28:38.000 --> 28:39.950
You can sleep in your wonderful car.

28:40.000 --> 28:40.950
I don't care.

28:41.000 --> 28:41.950
Good night.

28:42.000 --> 28:43.950
Luigi.

28:44.000 --> 28:46.950
Can you take me to our room, please?

28:47.000 --> 28:48.950
Of course, Nancy.

28:49.000 --> 28:50.950
This way, please.

28:51.000 --> 28:52.950
It's a nice room.

28:53.000 --> 28:54.950
Very comfortable beds.

28:55.000 --> 28:57.950
That sounds very nice.

28:58.000 --> 28:59.950
Come this way, please.

29:00.000 --> 29:01.950
We are back, Josephine.

29:02.000 --> 29:03.950
Mum, come on.

29:04.000 --> 29:04.950
But...

29:05.000 --> 29:05.950
Good night, Dad.

29:06.000 --> 29:07.950
Sleep well.

29:08.000 --> 29:09.950
Sweet dreams.

29:10.000 --> 29:11.000
But...

29:24.000 --> 29:25.950
I can't believe it.

29:26.000 --> 29:27.950
Where were you, Boris?

29:28.000 --> 29:29.000
Come here.

29:30.000 --> 29:31.950
Be quiet.

29:32.000 --> 29:34.950
Don't wake up the guests of the hotel.

29:35.000 --> 29:37.950
Be quiet.

29:38.000 --> 29:38.950
Come on.

29:39.000 --> 29:40.000
Get in the car.

29:45.000 --> 29:46.950
Just lay down, Doc.

29:47.000 --> 29:47.950
Be quiet.

29:48.000 --> 29:49.950
I don't believe it.

29:50.000 --> 29:54.950
The first night of the holiday, and I'm sleeping in the car with you.

29:55.000 --> 29:56.950
Stop barking.

29:57.000 --> 30:00.950
Can we try to sleep now, please, Boris?

30:01.000 --> 30:04.950
I am very, very tired.

30:05.000 --> 30:07.950
What's that noise?

30:08.000 --> 30:08.950
Go away.

30:09.000 --> 30:10.950
Be quiet, Doc.

30:11.000 --> 30:12.950
I'm going mad.

30:13.000 --> 30:15.950
Please open your window, sir.

30:16.000 --> 30:16.950
What?

30:17.000 --> 30:18.950
Oh, no.

30:19.000 --> 30:19.950
The police.

30:20.000 --> 30:20.950
What?

30:21.000 --> 30:23.950
Please open your window, sir.

30:24.000 --> 30:24.950
Yes, sir.

30:25.000 --> 30:28.000
Get off, Boris.

30:29.000 --> 30:31.950
No, Boris, not there.

