49:24.000 --> 49:25.950
The Middle Ages, before they invented the wheel.

49:26.000 --> 49:27.950
I ought to meet him.

49:28.000 --> 49:29.950
I don't care what you say.

49:30.000 --> 49:30.950
You do as I tell you.

49:31.000 --> 49:32.950
Nancy, speak to your daughter.

49:33.000 --> 49:33.950
Why ask me?

49:34.000 --> 49:35.950
You can speak to her yourself.

49:36.000 --> 49:37.950
I can go with Josie to meet him.

49:38.000 --> 49:39.950
Is that all right?

49:40.000 --> 49:40.950
Pete?

49:41.000 --> 49:43.950
I suppose so.

49:44.000 --> 49:45.950
But you know what your mother is like.

49:46.000 --> 49:47.950
She's very sensible.

49:48.000 --> 49:48.950
Hmm.

49:49.000 --> 49:49.950
I'm not so sure.

49:50.000 --> 49:50.950
Oh, no.

49:51.000 --> 49:51.950
Look.

49:52.000 --> 49:53.950
It's getting cloudy.

49:54.000 --> 49:55.950
Where's the sun gone?

49:56.000 --> 49:57.950
She think it's going to rain.

49:58.000 --> 50:00.950
Typical bloody, nothing black or weather.

50:01.000 --> 50:02.950
It's getting cold.

50:03.000 --> 50:04.950
Let's go back to the hotel.

50:05.000 --> 50:06.950
Mother, you can change out of that bikini.

50:07.000 --> 50:09.950
And then we can go to the pleasure beach this afternoon.

50:10.000 --> 50:12.950
Can we go on the ghost train together?

50:13.000 --> 50:14.950
I want to sit at the front.

50:15.000 --> 50:16.950
And I want some candy floss.

50:17.000 --> 50:19.950
She gets more like a child each day.

50:20.000 --> 50:22.950
I really think we must go and see her doctor when we get home.

50:23.000 --> 50:24.950
Pete, please don't say that.

50:25.000 --> 50:27.950
Can we just try to have a nice day?

50:28.000 --> 50:28.950
Yes, dear.

50:29.000 --> 50:30.950
Come on, everyone.

50:31.000 --> 50:32.950
Bring all our things.

50:33.000 --> 50:33.950
Ooh.

50:34.000 --> 50:34.950
Hurry up, Josie.

50:35.000 --> 50:36.950
Mom, bring the towels and the sunshade.

50:37.000 --> 50:38.950
Don't forget your sunglasses.

50:39.000 --> 50:39.950
Yes, Mom.

50:40.000 --> 50:40.950
Yes, Mom.

50:41.000 --> 50:42.950
Don't go on all the time.

50:43.000 --> 50:43.950
Thanks, Grand.

50:44.000 --> 50:47.000
We can sort something out when we're alone.

50:48.000 --> 50:49.950
Ooh, it's stuck to my nose.

50:50.000 --> 50:50.950
Help me, Nancy.

50:51.000 --> 50:51.950
Help me.

50:52.000 --> 50:52.950
It's OK, Grand.

50:53.000 --> 50:53.950
Let me help you.

50:54.000 --> 50:55.950
But candy floss is such fun.

50:56.000 --> 50:56.950
I like it.

50:57.000 --> 50:59.950
It is so sweet and sticky.

51:00.000 --> 51:01.950
Oh, Pete.

51:02.000 --> 51:05.950
It's so good to see Mother enjoying herself.

51:06.000 --> 51:07.950
I hope Josephine looks so good.

51:08.000 --> 51:08.950
It's so sweet.

51:09.000 --> 51:09.950
It's so sweet.

51:10.000 --> 51:10.950
Oh, Pete.

51:11.000 --> 51:14.000
It's so good to see Mother enjoying herself.

51:15.000 --> 51:17.950
I hope Josephine looks after us when we're old.

51:18.000 --> 51:19.950
I'm not so sure, Nancy.

51:20.000 --> 51:21.950
It's a different generation.

51:22.000 --> 51:23.950
What do we do when we're old?

51:24.000 --> 51:25.950
I don't know.

51:26.000 --> 51:26.950
I don't know.

51:27.000 --> 51:27.950
Come on, everyone.

51:28.000 --> 51:29.950
To the ghost train.

51:30.000 --> 51:31.950
I'm coming with you, Grand.

51:32.000 --> 51:33.950
Mom and Dad are so naff.

51:34.000 --> 51:34.950
You do go.

51:35.000 --> 51:38.950
We want to sit in a cafe and have a quiet cup of tea.

51:39.000 --> 51:40.950
We can make here in a couple of hours.

51:41.000 --> 51:42.950
You're on holiday.

51:43.000 --> 51:43.950
Relax.

51:44.000 --> 51:44.950
I'm fun.

51:45.000 --> 51:48.950
Going on a ghost train is not my idea of fun.

51:49.000 --> 51:49.950
You go.

51:50.000 --> 51:50.950
Okay.

51:51.000 --> 51:51.950
Grand?

51:52.000 --> 51:52.950
Yes, Josie.

51:53.000 --> 51:55.950
Can I ask you a big favor?

51:56.000 --> 51:58.950
Of course, my dear.

51:59.000 --> 52:01.950
Please, don't tell Mom and Dad.

52:02.000 --> 52:05.950
I want to go and see that barfly screen man.

52:06.000 --> 52:07.950
Is it okay?

52:08.000 --> 52:09.950
Of course, Josie.

52:10.000 --> 52:10.950
Have fun.

52:11.000 --> 52:13.950
You're only young once in your life.

52:14.000 --> 52:15.950
I'm happy by myself.

52:16.000 --> 52:21.950
Maybe there will be a lovely rich widower sitting next to me on the ghost train.

52:22.000 --> 52:23.950
Bye, Grand.

52:24.000 --> 52:25.000
Bye.

52:30.000 --> 52:31.950
Well, what a holiday.

52:32.000 --> 52:35.950
I hope the rest of the week is more peaceful and with no more disasters.

52:36.000 --> 52:38.950
Don't forget, we have to go home in your car.

52:39.000 --> 52:40.950
That is a disaster.

52:41.000 --> 52:41.950
Okay.

52:42.000 --> 52:42.950
Okay.

52:43.000 --> 52:43.950
Not again.

52:44.000 --> 52:44.950
Can we change the subject?

52:45.000 --> 52:45.950
You started it.

52:46.000 --> 52:47.950
You mentioned disasters, not me.

52:48.000 --> 52:49.950
You mentioned the car, not me.

52:50.000 --> 52:51.950
Not so loud.

52:52.000 --> 52:54.950
Everyone is listening to us.

52:55.000 --> 52:57.950
What's that in your teacup?

52:58.000 --> 52:59.950
It's moving.

53:00.000 --> 53:00.950
What?

53:01.000 --> 53:01.950
Where?

53:02.000 --> 53:02.950
Oh, no.

53:03.000 --> 53:03.950
